# Production API URL — fail-closed by default.
#
# No API origin is baked into the build. The approved Kaya API origin is injected
# at build time (CI reads the `VITE_API_URL` Actions variable; local Azure builds
# pass it on the command line). This matches the launch-hold posture: the web
# client must not ship pointing at an unreviewed/placeholder backend.
#
# When empty, the client uses relative paths (/api, /auth, /me, /admin), i.e. it
# expects a reverse proxy in front of it. The current Azure staging target is an
# INFO-ONLY static deploy (no clinical API), so empty is correct there.
#
# Azure base path: pass VITE_BASE_PATH=/ at build time (vite.config reads it from
# the process env, not this file). The GitHub Pages build uses /health-/ instead.
# IMPORTANT: Never use plain HTTP for health data. Always use HTTPS.
VITE_API_URL=
